**Unity UI Tool: QuickUI**

QuickUI is a user interface tool designed to facilitate the quick and easy creation of 2D game interfaces in Unity. It allows users to place pre-made UI elements and assets from a library, as well as custom UI elements and designs. The tool also includes functionality for testing and iterating on UI design within the Unity editor.

**Features:**

1. **UI Element Library:** A pre-built library of common UI elements, such as buttons, labels, and text inputs.
2. **Custom UI Element Support:** Users can create and add their own custom UI elements to the library.
3. **Drag-and-Drop Interface:** Users can easily drag and drop UI elements from the library onto the canvas.
4. **Real-time Preview:** The UI design is updated in real-time as users make changes.
5. **Testing and Iteration:** Users can test and iterate on their UI design within the Unity editor.
6. **Asset Management:** Users can manage their UI assets, including images, fonts, and other resources.

**Implementation:**

To implement QuickUI, we will create a custom Unity editor window that provides a user-friendly interface for creating and managing UI elements.

**Step 1: Create a new Unity project**

Create a new Unity project and set up a 2D game environment.

**Step 2: Create a custom editor window**

Create a new C# script in the Unity editor and name it `QuickUIEditorWindow`. This script will serve as the foundation for our custom editor window.

```csharp
using UnityEditor;
using UnityEngine;
using UnityEngine.UI;

public class QuickUIEditorWindow : EditorWindow
{
    // UI element library
    private List<UIElement> uiElements = new List<UIElement>();

    // Current UI design
    private Canvas canvas;

    // Draw the editor window
    [MenuItem("Window/QuickUI")]
    public static void ShowWindow()
    {
        GetWindow<QuickUIEditorWindow>("QuickUI");
    }

    private void OnGUI()
    {
        // Draw the UI element library
        DrawUIElementLibrary();

        // Draw the current UI design
        DrawCurrentUI();
    }

    private void DrawUIElementLibrary()
    {
        // Draw a list of UI elements
        foreach (var element in uiElements)
        {
            if (GUI.Button(new Rect(10, 10 + (element.Index * 20), 100, 20), element.Name))
            {
                // Add the UI element to the current UI design
                AddUIElement(element);
            }
        }
    }

    private void DrawCurrentUI()
    {
        // Draw the current UI design
        if (canvas != null)
        {
            // Draw a preview of the current UI design
            GUI.DrawTexture(new Rect(150, 10, 200, 200), canvas.renderTexture);
        }
    }

    private void AddUIElement(UIElement element)
    {
        // Add the UI element to the current UI design
        canvas = new GameObject("Canvas").AddComponent<Canvas>();
        var rectTransform = canvas.transform.Find("Canvas/Rect Transform");
        var image = rectTransform.Find("Image");
        var text = rectTransform.Find("Text");

        // Set the UI element's properties
        image.GetComponent<Image>().sprite = element.Sprite;
        text.GetComponent<Text>().text = element.Name;
    }
}
```

